# Keep secrets, local data, VCS metadata and dev clutter out of the Docker build
# context (D5-5). Without this, `COPY . .` baked the untracked .env (real
# provider keys) and instance/*.db (accounts, password hashes) into an image
# layer, and the app then loaded that .env at runtime.
#
# Patterns are anchored at the build context root (the repo root), unlike
# .gitignore: `*.pem` would only match top-level files, so the patterns meant
# for any depth start with `**/`.

# Secrets: every .env variant except the committed template, and key material.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
**/*.pem
**/*.key
**/*.p12
**/*.pfx
**/secrets.json
**/credentials.json

# Local databases, uploads and other instance data.
instance/
**/*.db

# VCS, CI and assistant/tooling scaffolding.
.git
.gitignore
.gitattributes
.github/
.autopilot/
.claude/
.superpowers/
CLAUDE.md
docs/DEPLOYMENT_PLAYBOOK.md
docs/superpowers/
docs/IMPLEMENTATION_PLAN.md
docs/CLOSEOUT.md
# Local audit reports, any capitalization (matching is case-sensitive).
**/*[Aa][Uu][Dd][Ii][Tt]*.md
.pre-commit-config.yaml

# Caches and virtual environments.
**/__pycache__/
**/*.pyc
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.coverage
htmlcov/
venv/
.venv/
node_modules/

# Not needed at runtime.
tests/
